## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

Requested 2026-08-30 by session tm-tournament-station-f7. Filed as an
ENHANCEMENT, not a bug — the reporter classified it that way themselves and
they are right: the LSP's answer is correct within the plugin and wrong about
intent.

## Gap

`info.toml` names an exports file:

    exports = "TournamentStation_Export.as"

The globals implementing that surface are called by OTHER plugins, never from
within the declaring plugin, so the unused analysis reports all of them as
unused. In the reporter's tree that is 4 warnings; for a library-shaped plugin
it would be considerably more.

## Why it is worth doing

The manifest already names the file, and `src/workspace/manifest.rs::validate`
already RESOLVES `exports` and `shared_exports` through
`crate::workspace::deps::resolve_plugin_file` (it errors when they do not
resolve — that is one of its three checks, see B040). So the information is
loaded, validated, and then not used for this. The wiring is short.

This is the same shape as B040 and B039: a capability that is computed and then
consumed by nobody. Worth stating plainly because it recurs.

## Work

Treat globals declared in a manifest-named exports file as ROOTS of the unused
analysis — reachable by definition, and anything they reach transitively is
reachable too.

Design questions to resolve before implementing, and record the decision in
this ticket:
- `exports` vs `shared_exports` — both root, or only one? Check what each
  actually means to Openplanet before deciding; do not guess from the name.
- Does rooting apply to the whole exports FILE, or only to declarations that
  match a signature in it? Prefer whole-file if the manifest names the file,
  since that is what the manifest asserts.
- Transitive reachability: a private helper called only by an exported
  function must stop being reported. This is the part that makes the feature
  actually useful rather than cosmetic.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)

Red: a fixture plugin whose `info.toml` names an exports file containing
`void PublicThing()`, called from nowhere in-plugin -> currently reported
unused.

Variants:
- exported global function -> not reported
- private helper reachable ONLY from an exported function -> not reported
- a global reachable from nothing at all, in a plugin that HAS exports ->
  STILL reported (the gate against rooting everything)
- plugin with no `exports` key -> behaviour completely unchanged
- `exports` naming a file that does not exist -> existing B040 error still
  fires, and the analysis does not panic or silently root nothing
- `shared_exports`, per the decision above
- exported CLASS and its methods, not just free functions

## Gate

FP fixture counts must not RISE; a drop in any fixture with an `exports` key is
the expected win. Two binaries, same machine, same time, absolute paths, both
formats.

## Related

B040 (manifest validation was dead code — this uses the same already-resolved
manifest data), B061 (the other false-unused report from the same session, but
a genuine BUG rather than an enhancement; keep them separate).

## Lane decision (coordinator, 2026-08-30)

Serialised last in lane `b060-b062-property-semantics`, after B060 and B061.
Shares `src/analysis/unused.rs` with B061. **Blocked until B059 merges.**

Sequenced last deliberately: B061 fixes what the unused analysis COUNTS as a
use, this ticket changes what it treats as a ROOT. Landing the counting fix
first means this ticket's fixture numbers are measured against correct
counting, so a drop here is attributable to rooting rather than to the two
changes interacting.